                                                "example_id": "e8827fb3-53f5-4147-be01-27306fcdb586",
                                                "sense_id": "f4f1e14e-c98f-30d8-9cee-b0269933d926",
                                                "text": "Will the Central Asiatics avail themselves of the communications opened for them in Europe? Will they accept, through the agency of Russia, the products of civilization, which we have neglected to convey to them, by the Indus and their own streams?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec8cbf88-597e-4608-9047-4d27bbb0fbda",
                                                "sense_id": "f4f1e14e-c98f-30d8-9cee-b0269933d926",
                                                "text": "My friend was obliged positively to force me to enter a booth, and, after the precious shivin (a kind of tea) was poured out, wishing to profit by the ecstatic feeling in which he found me, he asked me, chucklingly, “Now, then, what do you say to Bokhara Sherif (the noble)?” “It pleases me much,” I replied; and the Central Asiatic, although from Khokand, and an alien enemy, as his nation was at that moment at war with Bokhara, was nevertheless delighted to find that the capital of Turkestan had made such a conquest of me, and gave me his word that he would show me its finest features in the course of the following days."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e74788bd-bf96-40d2-9761-7a95921d1331",
                                                "sense_id": "f4f1e14e-c98f-30d8-9cee-b0269933d926",
                                                "text": "By describing him as a “Scythian shepherd,” Marlowe seizes the idea of the near contemporary Mongolians in the relatively unracialized image of the classical Scythians (who were neither Central Asiatics nor “shepherds,” though they were nomads)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e8912915-c98f-4818-b552-8b297265eb83",
                        "source_entry_id": "81c86cc2-f43c-3d46-ab5c-3684429ca791",
                        "source_sense_id": "b2425da5-ec37-3ff3-b533-751cc9cd50cf",
                        "target_lang_word": "Central Asiatic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Central Asiatic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb0b981b-8fdc-36cf-9a00-98f4c39b48ea",
                                        "entry_id": "13f45507-86d1-31a2-8f8e-a2ebdce15b7f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of Central Asian."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4beead95-7794-414e-afe6-34ed3a09861c",
                                                "sense_id": "eb0b981b-8fdc-36cf-9a00-98f4c39b48ea",
                                                "text": "The Central Asiatic race, the Mongol, the Tartar, when pure, revelled in tents and arms; plunder and the pomp of war was their whole aim."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b583e2c9-e5cd-4c67-83e1-667725d880f3",
                                                "sense_id": "eb0b981b-8fdc-36cf-9a00-98f4c39b48ea",
                                                "text": "The principal sets of Central Asiatic manufactures are Bokhara, Karshi, Yenghi Ürgendj, Khokand, and Namengan."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce757609-11ce-4bc0-b219-41d4ae22e653",
                                                "sense_id": "eb0b981b-8fdc-36cf-9a00-98f4c39b48ea",
                                                "text": "Ṭāq-i Bustān lies just east of Kirmānshāh, a town in western Irān on the so-called High Road that led from Mesopotamia through the central Zagros Mountains to Khurāsān, the crucially important Central Asiatic frontier of Arab conquest."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Central Asiatic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f4f1e14e-c98f-30d8-9cee-b0269933d926",
